### Rationale
H14 holds on the bench. The control copy (r1's load and store code with the maths removed) sustains 6.96 TB/s, and no other path beat it, so the r1 kernel stays as the candidate, unchanged. The 1-D bulk tests used the exact kernels and sizes listed in the findings. I did not run the 2-D TMA variant (d). With no variant beating the control by 3%, step 3 (adding RoPE and the tables to a faster path) was not triggered.

